SUMMARY:[Fintech D18] Real-Time Risk Engine (<100ms p95)\, Velocity Rules & Step-Up Auth (Project 3: Consumer App & Risk)
DESCRIPTION:PROJECT: Project 3: Consumer App & Risk (Day 18 of 30)\n\n1. DEEP THEORY & INDUSTRY STUDY (09:00 - 10:30):\nStudy: Data-driven fraud scoring under strict latency budgets (<100ms p95\; deterministic fallback on timeout: allow small\, step-up large). Starter rules: 10m/24h velocity\, 30-day median anomaly\, new counterparty\, new device <24h\, collect fan-out\, blacklist\, round-amount + night-time.\n\n2. CORE BACKEND & INFRA BUILD (10:30 - 13:30):\nBuild: Real-Time Risk Engine (POST /risk/score) evaluating weighted JSON rules in <100ms\; mapping score thresholds to ALLOW\, STEP_UP (extra mobile OTP or 30-min cooling delay with cancel button)\, or DECLINE\; full decision logging (fired rules\, weights\, inputs).
