SUMMARY:[Fintech D26] Dunning Engine\, Soft vs Hard Failures\, Grace Periods & Pay-Now Recovery (Project 4: Mandates & Subscriptions)
DESCRIPTION:PROJECT: Project 4: Mandates & Subscriptions (Day 26 of 30)\n\n1. DEEP THEORY & INDUSTRY STUDY (09:00 - 10:30):\nStudy: Soft failure (insufficient funds/timeout -> retry schedule Day 1\, 3\, 7\, each a fresh mandate execution with its own reference) vs Hard failure (mandate revoked/account closed -> halt immediately)\, PAST_DUE grace period\, and out-of-band recovery.\n\n2. CORE BACKEND & INFRA BUILD (10:30 - 13:30):\nBuild: Dunning Engine with configurable retry offsets\, templated customer dunning messages containing a Pay-Now Link (charges one-time via Project 2 Hosted Checkout -> clears cycle & restores ACTIVE)\, grace period expiry -> HALTED\, and recovery window reactivation.
